# Build-time PUBLIC env for the Astro build. Copy to .env for local work:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored; this file is not (see the `!.env.example` line in
# .gitignore). Nothing secret may be added to either — every PUBLIC_ value is
# inlined into the HTML the site ships. The Turnstile SECRET goes in .dev.vars
# locally and in a Pages secret in production; see README, Newsletter.

# Turnstile's "always passes, visible" TESTING key. Correct for local dev: the
# real widget only answers on jaan-io.pages.dev and jaan.io, so on localhost it
# would refuse to render and the form could never be submitted.
#
# The real site key lives in the PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY *repository variable*
# on GitHub, which is where CI — the only thing that builds a deploy — reads it
# from. Building this file's value and deploying it by hand would ship a form
# with no bot protection, so NewsletterSignup.astro fails a CI build that sees a
# testing key, and warns on a local one.
PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=1x00000000000000000000AA
